WEBVTT

00:00:00.337 --> 00:00:02.362
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> And just as you mentioned at the beginning of the show, you know, it’s

00:00:02.387 --> 00:00:07.883
– we all have stories, things, you know, your mum, the smell of cooking, it makes us feel safe and secure.

00:00:07.908 --> 00:00:11.861
And it might be a pair of shoes that your dad wore and the smell of the leather,

00:00:11.885 --> 00:00:14.090
or it might be the smell of your newborn child.

00:00:14.115 --> 00:00:16.397
I can remember the smell of my son when he was born.

00:00:16.722 --> 00:00:20.365
I’ve never been able to recreate it, but it’s, it’s the smell of new life for me.

00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:26.190
So, I think smell is a really powerful, memory evoking – it’s the nearest thing,

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.998
sits by the brain near the memory,

00:00:28.444 --> 00:00:32.866
which is why my dyslexia and my being able to create fragrance is

00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:37.232
what life took away with one hand, it gave me back with another because they sit side by side.